# CODEOWNERS: who owns which files. GitHub automatically requests a review
# from the owner when a PR touches their files.
#
# The last matching line wins. "Require review from code owners" is NOT
# turned on in the main ruleset: with a single maintainer and 0 required
# approvals it would block every PR. These lines still make ownership of
# the sensitive paths visible.

# Everything
*           @taracan

# Infrastructure (Terraform): changes reach AWS when applied from a laptop
/infra/     @taracan

# CI/CD workflows and repo settings: control deploys and the merge gate
/.github/   @taracan
